course: dictionary
lesson: 1120
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. «Hansel drops breadcrumbs to find the way home.» Here a breadcrumb is a tiny piece of bread. «Fish is coated in breadcrumbs before it is fried.» Here breadcrumbs are small bits of dried bread used for coating food. Ask: are we walking through a forest, or cooking dinner?
explain: Breadcrumb has a third meaning in computing. A breadcrumb trail is a line of links at the top of a website, like Home > Science > Plants, that shows you where you are. It works like Hansel's trail: it helps you find your way back.
explain: When you meet a word with several meanings, try each one in the sentence. Read the whole sentence again with your meaning in place of the word. If it still makes sense, you have found it. If not, try the next meaning.
fact: A breadcrumb is a tiny piece of bread.
fact: Breadcrumbs (plural) are very small bits of dried bread used to coat food, such as fish or chicken, before frying.
fact: A breadcrumb trail is a line of links on a website showing where you are, like Home > Science > Plants.
fact: In «Hansel and Gretel», an old fairy tale collected by the Brothers Grimm, Hansel drops breadcrumbs to find the way home, but the birds eat them.
fact: «Fish fingers» were first sold in Britain in 1955, and they are often breadcrumbed before cooking.
exercise: «Hansel drops breadcrumbs to find the way home.» What is a breadcrumb in this sentence? | *A tiny piece of bread | A small wooden path | A kind of bird | A map of the forest
exercise: «Cod is coated in breadcrumbs before it is fried.» What are the breadcrumbs used for here? | Building a trail to find the way home | *Coating food before frying | Showing where you are on a website | Feeding the birds in the park
exercise: What does a breadcrumb trail on a website show? | *Where you are, like Home > Science > Plants | The weather in Glasgow | The price of the things you bought | How many birds are in the park
test: In «The birds ate the breadcrumbs left on the path», what does breadcrumbs mean? | A coating for fish | A line of links on a website | *Tiny pieces of bread | A kind of bird
test: «Fish fingers are usually white fish, cut into blocks and breadcrumbed.» What does breadcrumbed mean? | Cut into small blocks of cake | Frozen in ice | Eaten raw with a fork | *Coated in dried bread crumbs before frying
exam: Which sentence uses breadcrumb in the computing sense? | The birds ate every breadcrumb | Coat the chicken in breadcrumbs | *The breadcrumb trail at the top of the page shows Home > Science > Plants | Hansel dropped breadcrumbs in the forest
